---@class aws.ec2.AllocateHostsRequest
---@field InstanceFamily? aws.ec2.String Specifies the instance family to be supported by the Dedicated Hosts. If you specify an instance family, the Dedicated Hosts support multiple instance types within that instance family.
---@field TagSpecifications? aws.ec2.TagSpecificationList The tags to apply to the Dedicated Host during creation.
---@field HostRecovery? aws.ec2.HostRecovery|string Indicates whether to enable or disable host recovery for the Dedicated Host. Host recovery is disabled by default. For more information, see Host recovery in the Amazon EC2 User Guide.
---@field OutpostArn? aws.ec2.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Amazon Web Services Outpost on which to allocate the Dedicated Host. If you specify OutpostArn, you can optionally specify AssetIds.
---@field HostMaintenance? aws.ec2.HostMaintenance|string Indicates whether to enable or disable host maintenance for the Dedicated Host. For more information, see Host maintenance in the Amazon EC2 User Guide.
---@field AssetIds? aws.ec2.AssetIdList The IDs of the Outpost hardware assets on which to allocate the Dedicated Hosts. Targeting specific hardware assets on an Outpost can help to minimize latency between your workloads. This parameter is supported only if you specify OutpostArn. If you are allocating the Dedicated Hosts in a Region, omit this parameter.
---@field AvailabilityZoneId? aws.ec2.AvailabilityZoneId The ID of the Availability Zone.
---@field CpuOptions? aws.ec2.HostCpuOptionsRequest The CPU configuration options to apply to the Dedicated Host.
