---Represents dimension values for capacity metrics, including resource identifiers, geographic information, and reservation details used for grouping and filtering capacity data.
---@class aws.ec2.CapacityManagerDimension
---@field ResourceRegion? aws.ec2.String The Amazon Web Services Region where the capacity resource is located.
---@field AvailabilityZoneId? aws.ec2.String The unique identifier of the Availability Zone where the capacity resource is located.
---@field AccountId? aws.ec2.String The Amazon Web Services account ID that owns the capacity resource.
---@field AccountName? aws.ec2.String The name of the Amazon Web Services account that owns the capacity resource. This dimension is only available when Organizations access is enabled for Capacity Manager.
---@field InstanceFamily? aws.ec2.String The EC2 instance family of the capacity resource.
---@field InstanceType? aws.ec2.String The specific EC2 instance type of the capacity resource.
---@field InstancePlatform? aws.ec2.String The platform or operating system of the instance.
---@field ReservationArn? aws.ec2.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the capacity reservation. This provides a unique identifier that can be used across Amazon Web Services services to reference the specific reservation.
---@field ReservationId? aws.ec2.String The unique identifier of the capacity reservation.
---@field ReservationType? aws.ec2.ReservationType The type of capacity reservation.
---@field ReservationCreateTimestamp? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The timestamp when the capacity reservation was originally created, in milliseconds since epoch. This differs from the start timestamp as reservations can be created before they become active.
---@field ReservationStartTimestamp? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The timestamp when the capacity reservation becomes active and available for use, in milliseconds since epoch. This is when the reservation begins providing capacity.
---@field ReservationEndTimestamp? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The timestamp when the capacity reservation expires and is no longer available, in milliseconds since epoch. After this time, the reservation will not provide any capacity.
---@field ReservationEndDateType? aws.ec2.ReservationEndDateType The type of end date for the capacity reservation. This indicates whether the reservation has a fixed end date, is open-ended, or follows a specific termination pattern.
---@field Tenancy? aws.ec2.CapacityTenancy The tenancy of the EC2 instances associated with this capacity dimension. Valid values are 'default' for shared tenancy, 'dedicated' for dedicated instances, or 'host' for dedicated hosts.
---@field ReservationState? aws.ec2.ReservationState The current state of the capacity reservation.
---@field ReservationInstanceMatchCriteria? aws.ec2.String The instance matching criteria for the capacity reservation, determining how instances are matched to the reservation.
---@field ReservationUnusedFinancialOwner? aws.ec2.String The Amazon Web Services account ID that is financially responsible for unused capacity reservation costs.
---@field Tags? aws.ec2.CapacityManagerTagDimensionSet The tags associated with the capacity resource, represented as key-value pairs. Only tags that have been activated for monitoring via UpdateCapacityManagerMonitoredTagKeys are included.

---Describes a tag key that is being monitored by Capacity Manager, including its activation status and the earliest available data point.
