---Describes a Capacity Reservation.
---@class aws.ec2.CapacityReservation
---@field CapacityReservationId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the Capacity Reservation.
---@field OwnerId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the Amazon Web Services account that owns the Capacity Reservation.
---@field CapacityReservationArn? aws.ec2.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Capacity Reservation.
---@field AvailabilityZoneId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the Availability Zone in which the capacity is reserved.
---@field InstanceType? aws.ec2.String The type of instance for which the Capacity Reservation reserves capacity.
---@field InstancePlatform? aws.ec2.CapacityReservationInstancePlatform The type of operating system for which the Capacity Reservation reserves capacity.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.ec2.String The Availability Zone in which the capacity is reserved.
---@field Tenancy? aws.ec2.CapacityReservationTenancy Indicates the tenancy of the Capacity Reservation. A Capacity Reservation can have one of the following tenancy settings:
---@field TotalInstanceCount? aws.ec2.Integer The total number of instances for which the Capacity Reservation reserves capacity.
---@field AvailableInstanceCount? aws.ec2.Integer The remaining capacity. Indicates the number of instances that can be launched in the Capacity Reservation.
---@field EbsOptimized? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether the Capacity Reservation supports EBS-optimized instances. This optimization provides dedicated throughput to Amazon EBS and an optimized configuration stack to provide optimal I/O performance. This optimization isn't available with all instance types. Additional usage charges apply when using an EBS- optimized instance.
---@field EphemeralStorage? aws.ec2.Boolean Deprecated.
---@field State? aws.ec2.CapacityReservationState The current state of the Capacity Reservation. A Capacity Reservation can be in one of the following states:
---@field StartDate? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The date and time the Capacity Reservation was started.
---@field EndDate? aws.ec2.DateTime The date and time the Capacity Reservation expires. When a Capacity Reservation expires, the reserved capacity is released and you can no longer launch instances into it. The Capacity Reservation's state changes to expired when it reaches its end date and time.
---@field EndDateType? aws.ec2.EndDateType Indicates the way in which the Capacity Reservation ends. A Capacity Reservation can have one of the following end types:
---@field InstanceMatchCriteria? aws.ec2.InstanceMatchCriteria Indicates the type of instance launches that the Capacity Reservation accepts. The options include:
---@field CreateDate? aws.ec2.DateTime The date and time the Capacity Reservation was created.
---@field Tags? aws.ec2.TagList Any tags assigned to the Capacity Reservation.
---@field OutpostArn? aws.ec2.OutpostArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Outpost on which the Capacity Reservation was created.
---@field CapacityReservationFleetId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the Capacity Reservation Fleet to which the Capacity Reservation belongs. Only valid for Capacity Reservations that were created by a Capacity Reservation Fleet.
---@field PlacementGroupArn? aws.ec2.PlacementGroupArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the cluster placement group in which the Capacity Reservation was created. For more information, see Capacity Reservations for cluster placement groups in the Amazon EC2 User Guide.
---@field CapacityAllocations? aws.ec2.CapacityAllocations Information about instance capacity usage.
---@field ReservationType? aws.ec2.CapacityReservationType The type of Capacity Reservation.
---@field UnusedReservationBillingOwnerId? aws.ec2.AccountID The ID of the Amazon Web Services account to which billing of the unused capacity of the Capacity Reservation is assigned.
---@field CommitmentInfo? aws.ec2.CapacityReservationCommitmentInfo Information about your commitment for a future-dated Capacity Reservation.
---@field DeliveryPreference? aws.ec2.CapacityReservationDeliveryPreference The delivery method for a future-dated Capacity Reservation. incremental indicates that the requested capacity is delivered in addition to any running instances and reserved capacity that you have in your account at the requested date and time.
---@field CapacityBlockId? aws.ec2.CapacityBlockId The ID of the Capacity Block.
---@field Interruptible? aws.ec2.BoxedBoolean Indicates whether this Capacity Reservation is interruptible, meaning instances may be terminated when the owner reclaims capacity.
---@field InterruptibleCapacityAllocation? aws.ec2.InterruptibleCapacityAllocation Contains allocation details for interruptible reservations, including current allocated instances and target instance counts within the interruptibleCapacityAllocation object.
---@field InterruptionInfo? aws.ec2.InterruptionInfo Information about the interruption configuration and association with the source reservation for interruptible Capacity Reservations.
---@field AdjustmentStatus? aws.ec2.CapacityReservationAdjustmentStatus The status of the most recent modification to the Capacity Reservation. A Capacity Reservation can have one of the following adjustment statuses:
---@field AdjustmentDetails? aws.ec2.CapacityReservationAdjustmentDetails The configuration that the Capacity Reservation will have after the requested adjustment is applied.
---@field OriginalStartDate? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The start date that you originally requested for the Capacity Reservation, in the ISO8601 format in the UTC time zone (YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ). This value doesn't change when you push out the start date.
---@field ZeroSizePreference? aws.ec2.ZeroSizePreference The zero-size preference configured for the interruptible Capacity Reservation. A value of retain keeps the interruptible Capacity Reservation active at zero capacity when you reduce its allocation to zero. A value of default cancels the interruptible Capacity Reservation when you reduce its allocation to zero.
---@field LaunchStatus? aws.ec2.CapacityReservationLaunchStatus Only supported for UltraServers. Indicates whether you can launch instances into the Capacity Reservation. A Capacity Reservation can have the following launch statuses: launchable - You can launch instances into the Capacity Reservation. unlaunchable - You can't launch instances into the Capacity Reservation. For example, the Capacity Reservation is not active.

