---@class aws.ec2.CreateApplicationStatusCheckRequest
---@field HealthCheckPaths? aws.ec2.HealthCheckPathRequestList The health check paths to use for the application status check. Health check paths define the network path from a source subnet to one or more destination subnets for cross-Availability Zone or Availability Zone to Local Zone health checking. If omitted, health checks are performed in the same subnet as the instance.
---@field Aggregation? aws.ec2.AggregationStatusEnum|string The aggregation setting for the application status check. When set to included, the result of this check contributes to the instance-level application status reported by DescribeApplicationStatus. When set to excluded, the check runs independently and does not affect the instance-level status. Valid values: included | excluded.
---@field Protocol aws.ec2.NetworkProtocolEnum|string The protocol to use for the health check. Valid values: http | https.
---@field Port aws.ec2.PortNumber The port to use for the health check. Valid values: 1 to 65535.
---@field Path? aws.ec2.String The URL path to use for the health check HTTP request (for example, /health or /status).
---@field DeviceIndex? aws.ec2.Integer The index of the network device to use for the health check. The value must be greater than or equal to 0.
---@field IpVersion? aws.ec2.IpVersionEnum|string The IP version to use for the health check. Valid values: ipv4 and ipv6.
---@field IpScope? aws.ec2.IpScopeEnum|string The IP scope to use for the health check. Valid value: private.
---@field Interval? aws.ec2.Integer The interval, in seconds, between health checks. Valid value: 60.
---@field Timeout? aws.ec2.Integer The amount of time, in seconds, to wait for a health check response before considering it failed. Valid values: 1 to 30. The value must be less than Interval.
---@field FailureThreshold? aws.ec2.Integer The number of consecutive failed health checks before the application status is considered impaired. The value must be greater than 0.
---@field SuccessThreshold? aws.ec2.Integer The number of consecutive successful health checks before the application status is considered healthy. The value must be greater than 0.
---@field StatusCodeMatcher? aws.ec2.String The HTTP status codes that indicate a successful health check response. Specify a comma-separated list of individual status codes or ranges, for example, 200,202,300-399. For a range, the first value must be less than the second value. Maximum length: 64 characters. Default: 200.
---@field InitializationGracePeriodSeconds? aws.ec2.InitializationGracePeriodSeconds The number of seconds to wait before starting health checks after an instance is launched. Valid values: 1 to 600.
---@field TagSpecifications? aws.ec2.TagSpecificationList The tags to apply to the application status check.
---@field ClientToken? aws.ec2.String A unique, case-sensitive identifier that you provide to ensure that the operation completes no more than one time. If you retry a request with the same token, the service ignores the request but does not return an error. For more information, see Ensuring idempotency.
---@field DryRun? aws.ec2.Boolean Checks whether you have the required permissions for the operation, without actually making the request, and provides an error response. If you have the required permissions, the error response is DryRunOperation. Otherwise, it is UnauthorizedOperation.

