---@class aws.ec2.CreateClientVpnEndpointRequest
---@field ClientCidrBlock? aws.ec2.String The IPv4 address range, in CIDR notation, from which to assign client IP addresses. The address range cannot overlap with the local CIDR of the VPC in which the associated subnet is located, or the routes that you add manually. The address range cannot be changed after the Client VPN endpoint has been created. Client CIDR range must have a size of at least /22 and must not be greater than /12.
---@field ServerCertificateArn aws.ec2.String The ARN of the server certificate. For more information, see the Certificate Manager User Guide.
---@field AuthenticationOptions aws.ec2.ClientVpnAuthenticationRequestList Information about the authentication method to be used to authenticate clients.
---@field ConnectionLogOptions aws.ec2.ConnectionLogOptions Information about the client connection logging options.
---@field DnsServers? aws.ec2.ValueStringList Information about the DNS servers to be used for DNS resolution. A Client VPN endpoint can have up to two DNS servers. If no DNS server is specified, the DNS address configured on the device is used for the DNS server.
---@field TransportProtocol? aws.ec2.TransportProtocol|string The transport protocol to be used by the VPN session.
---@field VpnPort? aws.ec2.Integer The port number to assign to the Client VPN endpoint for TCP and UDP traffic.
---@field Description? aws.ec2.String A brief description of the Client VPN endpoint.
---@field SplitTunnel? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether split-tunnel is enabled on the Client VPN endpoint.
