---Describes a block device for an EBS volume.
---@class aws.ec2.EbsBlockDevice
---@field DeleteOnTermination? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether the EBS volume is deleted on instance termination. For more information, see Preserving Amazon EBS volumes on instance termination in the Amazon EC2 User Guide.
---@field Iops? aws.ec2.Integer The number of I/O operations per second (IOPS). For gp3, io1, and io2 volumes, this represents the number of IOPS that are provisioned for the volume. For gp2 volumes, this represents the baseline performance of the volume and the rate at which the volume accumulates I/O credits for bursting.
---@field SnapshotId? aws.ec2.SnapshotId The ID of the snapshot.
---@field VolumeSize? aws.ec2.Integer The size of the volume, in GiBs. You must specify either a snapshot ID or a volume size. If you specify a snapshot, the default is the snapshot size. You can specify a volume size that is equal to or larger than the snapshot size.
---@field VolumeType? aws.ec2.VolumeType|string The volume type. For more information, see Amazon EBS volume types in the Amazon EBS User Guide.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.ec2.String Identifier (key ID, key alias, key ARN, or alias ARN) of the customer managed KMS key to use for EBS encryption.
---@field Throughput? aws.ec2.Integer The throughput that the volume supports, in MiB/s.
---@field OutpostArn? aws.ec2.String The ARN of the Outpost on which the snapshot is stored.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.ec2.String The Availability Zone where the EBS volume will be created (for example, us-east-1a).
---@field Encrypted? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether the encryption state of an EBS volume is changed while being restored from a backing snapshot. The effect of setting the encryption state to true depends on the volume origin (new or from a snapshot), starting encryption state, ownership, and whether encryption by default is enabled. For more information, see Amazon EBS encryption in the Amazon EBS User Guide.
---@field VolumeInitializationRate? aws.ec2.Integer Specifies the Amazon EBS Provisioned Rate for Volume Initialization (volume initialization rate), in MiB/s, at which to download the snapshot blocks from Amazon S3 to the volume. This is also known as volume initialization. Specifying a volume initialization rate ensures that the volume is initialized at a predictable and consistent rate after creation. For more information, see Initialize Amazon ...
---@field AvailabilityZoneId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the Availability Zone where the EBS volume will be created (for example, use1-az1).
