---Describes a network interface.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceNetworkInterfaceSpecification
---@field AssociatePublicIpAddress? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether to assign a public IPv4 address to an instance you launch in a VPC. The public IP address can only be assigned to a network interface for eth0, and can only be assigned to a new network interface, not an existing one. You cannot specify more than one network interface in the request. If launching into a default subnet, the default value is true.
---@field DeleteOnTermination? aws.ec2.Boolean If set to true, the interface is deleted when the instance is terminated. You can specify true only if creating a new network interface when launching an instance.
---@field Description? aws.ec2.String The description of the network interface. Applies only if creating a network interface when launching an instance.
---@field DeviceIndex? aws.ec2.Integer The position of the network interface in the attachment order. A primary network interface has a device index of 0.
---@field Groups? aws.ec2.SecurityGroupIdStringList The IDs of the security groups for the network interface. Applies only if creating a network interface when launching an instance.
---@field Ipv6AddressCount? aws.ec2.Integer A number of IPv6 addresses to assign to the network interface. Amazon EC2 chooses the IPv6 addresses from the range of the subnet. You cannot specify this option and the option to assign specific IPv6 addresses in the same request. You can specify this option if you've specified a minimum number of instances to launch.
---@field Ipv6Addresses? aws.ec2.InstanceIpv6AddressList The IPv6 addresses to assign to the network interface. You cannot specify this option and the option to assign a number of IPv6 addresses in the same request. You cannot specify this option if you've specified a minimum number of instances to launch.
---@field NetworkInterfaceId? aws.ec2.NetworkInterfaceId The ID of the network interface.
---@field PrivateIpAddress? aws.ec2.String The private IPv4 address of the network interface. Applies only if creating a network interface when launching an instance. You cannot specify this option if you're launching more than one instance in a RunInstances request.
---@field PrivateIpAddresses? aws.ec2.PrivateIpAddressSpecificationList The private IPv4 addresses to assign to the network interface. Only one private IPv4 address can be designated as primary. You cannot specify this option if you're launching more than one instance in a RunInstances request.
---@field SecondaryPrivateIpAddressCount? aws.ec2.Integer The number of secondary private IPv4 addresses. You can’t specify this parameter and also specify a secondary private IP address using the PrivateIpAddress parameter.
---@field SubnetId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the subnet associated with the network interface. Applies only if creating a network interface when launching an instance.
---@field AssociateCarrierIpAddress? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether to assign a carrier IP address to the network interface.
---@field InterfaceType? aws.ec2.String The type of network interface.
---@field NetworkCardIndex? aws.ec2.Integer The index of the network card. Some instance types support multiple network cards. The primary network interface must be assigned to network card index 0. The default is network card index 0.
---@field Ipv4Prefixes? aws.ec2.Ipv4PrefixList The IPv4 delegated prefixes to be assigned to the network interface. You cannot use this option if you use the Ipv4PrefixCount option.
---@field Ipv4PrefixCount? aws.ec2.Integer The number of IPv4 delegated prefixes to be automatically assigned to the network interface. You cannot use this option if you use the Ipv4Prefix option.
---@field Ipv6Prefixes? aws.ec2.Ipv6PrefixList The IPv6 delegated prefixes to be assigned to the network interface. You cannot use this option if you use the Ipv6PrefixCount option.
