---The instance details to specify which volumes should be snapshotted.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceSpecification
---@field InstanceId aws.ec2.InstanceIdWithVolumeResolver The instance to specify which volumes should be snapshotted.
---@field ExcludeBootVolume? aws.ec2.Boolean Excludes the root volume from being snapshotted.
---@field ExcludeDataVolumeIds? aws.ec2.VolumeIdStringList The IDs of the data (non-root) volumes to exclude from the multi-volume snapshot set. If you specify the ID of the root volume, the request fails. To exclude the root volume, use ExcludeBootVolume.

---Describes the current state of an instance.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceState
---@field Code? aws.ec2.Integer The state of the instance as a 16-bit unsigned integer.
---@field Name? aws.ec2.InstanceStateName The current state of the instance.

---Describes an instance state change.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceStateChange
---@field InstanceId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the instance.
---@field CurrentState? aws.ec2.InstanceState The current state of the instance.
---@field PreviousState? aws.ec2.InstanceState The previous state of the instance.

---@alias aws.ec2.InstanceStateChangeList aws.ec2.InstanceStateChange[]

---@alias aws.ec2.InstanceStateName "pending"|"running"|"shutting-down"|"terminated"|"stopping"|"stopped"

---Describes the status of an instance, including system status, instance status, attached EBS status, application status, and performance status.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceStatus
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.ec2.String The Availability Zone of the instance.
---@field AvailabilityZoneId? aws.ec2.AvailabilityZoneId The ID of the Availability Zone of the instance.
---@field OutpostArn? aws.ec2.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Outpost.
---@field Operator? aws.ec2.OperatorResponse The service provider that manages the instance.
---@field Events? aws.ec2.InstanceStatusEventList Any scheduled events associated with the instance.
---@field InstanceId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the instance.
---@field InstanceState? aws.ec2.InstanceState The intended state of the instance. DescribeInstanceStatus requires that an instance be in the running state.
---@field InstanceStatus? aws.ec2.InstanceStatusSummary Reports impaired functionality that stems from issues internal to the instance, such as impaired reachability.
---@field SystemStatus? aws.ec2.InstanceStatusSummary Reports impaired functionality that stems from issues related to the systems that support an instance, such as hardware failures and network connectivity problems.
---@field AttachedEbsStatus? aws.ec2.EbsStatusSummary Reports impaired functionality that stems from an attached Amazon EBS volume that is unreachable and unable to complete I/O operations.
---@field ApplicationStatus? aws.ec2.ApplicationStatusSummary Reports the application-level health status for the instance.
---@field PerformanceStatus? aws.ec2.PerformanceStatusSummary Reports the performance-related health status for the instance. This information is returned only when performance status checks are enabled for the instance.

---Describes the instance status.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceStatusDetails
---@field ImpairedSince? aws.ec2.DateTime The time when a status check failed. For an instance that was launched and impaired, this is the time when the instance was launched.
---@field Name? aws.ec2.StatusName The type of instance status.
---@field Status? aws.ec2.StatusType The status.

---@alias aws.ec2.InstanceStatusDetailsList aws.ec2.InstanceStatusDetails[]

---Describes a scheduled event for an instance.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceStatusEvent
---@field InstanceEventId? aws.ec2.InstanceEventId The ID of the event.
---@field Code? aws.ec2.EventCode The event code.
---@field Description? aws.ec2.String A description of the event.
---@field NotAfter? aws.ec2.DateTime The latest scheduled end time for the event.
---@field NotBefore? aws.ec2.DateTime The earliest scheduled start time for the event.
---@field NotBeforeDeadline? aws.ec2.DateTime The deadline for starting the event.

---@alias aws.ec2.InstanceStatusEventList aws.ec2.InstanceStatusEvent[]

---@alias aws.ec2.InstanceStatusList aws.ec2.InstanceStatus[]

---Describes the status of an instance.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceStatusSummary
---@field Details? aws.ec2.InstanceStatusDetailsList The system instance health or application instance health.
---@field Status? aws.ec2.SummaryStatus The status.

---@alias aws.ec2.InstanceStorageEncryptionSupport "unsupported"|"required"

---@alias aws.ec2.InstanceStorageFlag boolean

---Describes the instance store features that are supported by the instance type.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceStorageInfo
---@field TotalSizeInGB? aws.ec2.DiskSize The total size of the disks, in GB.
---@field Disks? aws.ec2.DiskInfoList Describes the disks that are available for the instance type.
---@field NvmeSupport? aws.ec2.EphemeralNvmeSupport Indicates whether non-volatile memory express (NVMe) is supported.
---@field EncryptionSupport? aws.ec2.InstanceStorageEncryptionSupport Indicates whether data is encrypted at rest.

---@alias aws.ec2.InstanceTagKeySet aws.ec2.String[]

---Describes the registered tag keys for the current Region.
---@class aws.ec2.InstanceTagNotificationAttribute
---@field InstanceTagKeys? aws.ec2.InstanceTagKeySet The registered tag keys.
---@field IncludeAllTagsOfInstance? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates wheter all tag keys in the current Region are registered to appear in scheduled event notifications. true indicates that all tag keys in the current Region are registered.

