---ENA Express uses Amazon Web Services Scalable Reliable Datagram (SRD) technology to increase the maximum bandwidth used per stream and minimize tail latency of network traffic between EC2 instances. With ENA Express, you can communicate between two EC2 instances in the same subnet within the same account, or in different accounts. Both sending and receiving instances must have ENA Express enabled.
---@class aws.ec2.LaunchTemplateEnaSrdSpecification
---@field EnaSrdEnabled? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether ENA Express is enabled for the network interface.
---@field EnaSrdUdpSpecification? aws.ec2.LaunchTemplateEnaSrdUdpSpecification Configures ENA Express for UDP network traffic.

---ENA Express is compatible with both TCP and UDP transport protocols. When it's enabled, TCP traffic automatically uses it. However, some UDP-based applications are designed to handle network packets that are out of order, without a need for retransmission, such as live video broadcasting or other near-real-time applications. For UDP traffic, you can specify whether to use ENA Express, based on you...
---@class aws.ec2.LaunchTemplateEnaSrdUdpSpecification
---@field EnaSrdUdpEnabled? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether UDP traffic to and from the instance uses ENA Express. To specify this setting, you must first enable ENA Express.

