---The Amazon Web Services Site-to-Site VPN tunnel options to modify.
---@class aws.ec2.ModifyVpnTunnelOptionsSpecification
---@field TunnelInsideCidr? aws.ec2.String The range of inside IPv4 addresses for the tunnel. Any specified CIDR blocks must be unique across all VPN connections that use the same virtual private gateway.
---@field TunnelInsideIpv6Cidr? aws.ec2.String The range of inside IPv6 addresses for the tunnel. Any specified CIDR blocks must be unique across all VPN connections that use the same transit gateway.
---@field PreSharedKey? aws.ec2.preSharedKey|distilled.Secret The pre-shared key (PSK) to establish initial authentication between the virtual private gateway and the customer gateway.
---@field Phase1LifetimeSeconds? aws.ec2.Integer The lifetime for phase 1 of the IKE negotiation, in seconds.
---@field Phase2LifetimeSeconds? aws.ec2.Integer The lifetime for phase 2 of the IKE negotiation, in seconds.
---@field RekeyMarginTimeSeconds? aws.ec2.Integer The margin time, in seconds, before the phase 2 lifetime expires, during which the Amazon Web Services side of the VPN connection performs an IKE rekey. The exact time of the rekey is randomly selected based on the value for RekeyFuzzPercentage.
---@field RekeyFuzzPercentage? aws.ec2.Integer The percentage of the rekey window (determined by RekeyMarginTimeSeconds) during which the rekey time is randomly selected.
---@field ReplayWindowSize? aws.ec2.Integer The number of packets in an IKE replay window.
---@field DPDTimeoutSeconds? aws.ec2.Integer The number of seconds after which a DPD timeout occurs. A DPD timeout of 40 seconds means that the VPN endpoint will consider the peer dead 30 seconds after the first failed keep-alive.
---@field DPDTimeoutAction? aws.ec2.String The action to take after DPD timeout occurs. Specify restart to restart the IKE initiation. Specify clear to end the IKE session.
---@field Phase1EncryptionAlgorithms? aws.ec2.Phase1EncryptionAlgorithmsRequestList One or more encryption algorithms that are permitted for the VPN tunnel for phase 1 IKE negotiations.
---@field Phase2EncryptionAlgorithms? aws.ec2.Phase2EncryptionAlgorithmsRequestList One or more encryption algorithms that are permitted for the VPN tunnel for phase 2 IKE negotiations.
---@field Phase1IntegrityAlgorithms? aws.ec2.Phase1IntegrityAlgorithmsRequestList One or more integrity algorithms that are permitted for the VPN tunnel for phase 1 IKE negotiations.
---@field Phase2IntegrityAlgorithms? aws.ec2.Phase2IntegrityAlgorithmsRequestList One or more integrity algorithms that are permitted for the VPN tunnel for phase 2 IKE negotiations.
---@field Phase1DHGroupNumbers? aws.ec2.Phase1DHGroupNumbersRequestList One or more Diffie-Hellman group numbers that are permitted for the VPN tunnel for phase 1 IKE negotiations.
---@field Phase2DHGroupNumbers? aws.ec2.Phase2DHGroupNumbersRequestList One or more Diffie-Hellman group numbers that are permitted for the VPN tunnel for phase 2 IKE negotiations.
---@field IKEVersions? aws.ec2.IKEVersionsRequestList The IKE versions that are permitted for the VPN tunnel.
---@field StartupAction? aws.ec2.String The action to take when the establishing the tunnel for the VPN connection. By default, your customer gateway device must initiate the IKE negotiation and bring up the tunnel. Specify start for Amazon Web Services to initiate the IKE negotiation.
---@field LogOptions? aws.ec2.VpnTunnelLogOptionsSpecification Options for logging VPN tunnel activity.
---@field EnableTunnelLifecycleControl? aws.ec2.Boolean Turn on or off tunnel endpoint lifecycle control feature.

