---Describes the options for instance hostnames.
---@class aws.ec2.PrivateDnsNameOptionsOnLaunch
---@field HostnameType? aws.ec2.HostnameType The type of hostname for EC2 instances. For IPv4 only subnets, an instance DNS name must be based on the instance IPv4 address. For IPv6 only subnets, an instance DNS name must be based on the instance ID. For dual-stack subnets, you can specify whether DNS names use the instance IPv4 address or the instance ID.
---@field EnableResourceNameDnsARecord? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether to respond to DNS queries for instance hostnames with DNS A records.
---@field EnableResourceNameDnsAAAARecord? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether to respond to DNS queries for instance hostname with DNS AAAA records.

---Describes the options for instance hostnames.
---@class aws.ec2.PrivateDnsNameOptionsRequest
---@field HostnameType? aws.ec2.HostnameType|string The type of hostname for EC2 instances. For IPv4 only subnets, an instance DNS name must be based on the instance IPv4 address. For IPv6 only subnets, an instance DNS name must be based on the instance ID. For dual-stack subnets, you can specify whether DNS names use the instance IPv4 address or the instance ID.
---@field EnableResourceNameDnsARecord? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether to respond to DNS queries for instance hostnames with DNS A records.
---@field EnableResourceNameDnsAAAARecord? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether to respond to DNS queries for instance hostnames with DNS AAAA records.

