---@field Cidr aws.ec2.String The public IPv4 or IPv6 address range, in CIDR notation. The most specific IPv4 prefix that you can specify is /24. The most specific IPv6 address range that you can bring is /48 for CIDRs that are publicly advertisable and /56 for CIDRs that are not publicly advertisable. The address range cannot overlap with another address range that you've brought to this or another Region.
---@field CidrAuthorizationContext? aws.ec2.CidrAuthorizationContext A signed document that proves that you are authorized to bring the specified IP address range to Amazon using BYOIP.
---@field PubliclyAdvertisable? aws.ec2.Boolean (IPv6 only) Indicate whether the address range will be publicly advertised to the internet.
---@field Description? aws.ec2.String A description for the address range and the address pool.
---@field DryRun? aws.ec2.Boolean Checks whether you have the required permissions for the action, without actually making the request, and provides an error response. If you have the required permissions, the error response is DryRunOperation. Otherwise, it is UnauthorizedOperation.
---@field PoolTagSpecifications? aws.ec2.TagSpecificationList The tags to apply to the address pool.
---@field MultiRegion? aws.ec2.Boolean Reserved.
---@field NetworkBorderGroup? aws.ec2.String If you have Local Zones enabled, you can choose a network border group for Local Zones when you provision and advertise a BYOIPv4 CIDR. Choose the network border group carefully as the EIP and the Amazon Web Services resource it is associated with must reside in the same network border group.

---@class aws.ec2.ProvisionByoipCidrResult
---@field ByoipCidr? aws.ec2.ByoipCidr Information about the address range.

