---Describes the fallback behavior for an EC2 Fleet that uses reserved capacity when the reserved capacity is not enough to meet the target capacity. If you don't specify fallback options, EC2 Fleet does not fall back to any other market type after the specified reservation types are exhausted.
---@class aws.ec2.ReservedCapacityFallbackOptionsRequest
---@field MarketTypes? aws.ec2.ReservedCapacityFallbackMarketTypeList The instance purchasing options to fall back to when the reserved capacity is not enough to meet the target capacity. The only supported value is on-demand, which launches On-Demand Instances to fulfill the remaining target capacity.

---Defines EC2 Fleet preferences for utilizing reserved capacity when DefaultTargetCapacityType is set to reserved-capacity. EC2 Fleet can fulfill reserved capacity using On-Demand Capacity Reservations, Capacity Blocks for ML, and interruptible Capacity Reservations.
---@class aws.ec2.ReservedCapacityOptions
---@field AllocationStrategy? aws.ec2.ReservedCapacityAllocationStrategy The strategy that determines the order in which EC2 Fleet launches instances across the reservation types that you specify. The only supported value is prioritized, which launches instances in the priority order that you specify in your launch template overrides. If you don't specify an allocation strategy, instances are launched in a random order.
---@field ReservationTypes? aws.ec2.ReservationTypeList The types of Capacity Reservations used for fulfilling the EC2 Fleet request.
---@field ReservedCapacityFallbackOptions? aws.ec2.ReservedCapacityFallbackOptions The fallback behavior for the EC2 Fleet when there is not enough reserved capacity available to meet the target capacity.

---Defines EC2 Fleet preferences for utilizing reserved capacity when DefaultTargetCapacityType is set to reserved-capacity. EC2 Fleet can fulfill reserved capacity using On-Demand Capacity Reservations, Capacity Blocks for ML, and interruptible Capacity Reservations.
---@class aws.ec2.ReservedCapacityOptionsRequest
---@field AllocationStrategy? aws.ec2.ReservedCapacityAllocationStrategy|string The strategy that determines the order in which EC2 Fleet launches instances across the reservation types that you specify. The only supported value is prioritized, which launches instances in the priority order that you specify in your launch template overrides. If you don't specify an allocation strategy, instances are launched in a random order.
---@field ReservationTypes? aws.ec2.ReservationTypeListRequest The types of Capacity Reservations to use for fulfilling the EC2 Fleet request. This is an ordered list: EC2 Fleet attempts to launch instances into each Capacity Reservation type in the order that you specify them before moving on to the next type.
---@field CapacityReservationTarget? aws.ec2.FleetCapacityReservationTargetRequest The Capacity Reservations or Capacity Reservation Resource Groups to use for fulfilling the EC2 Fleet request. You can specify Capacity Reservation IDs or a Capacity Reservation Resource Group ARN, but not both.
---@field ReservedCapacityFallbackOptions? aws.ec2.ReservedCapacityFallbackOptionsRequest The fallback behavior for the EC2 Fleet when there is not enough reserved capacity available to meet the target capacity. This member takes a ReservedCapacityFallbackOptionsRequest structure, in which you set MarketTypes to the instance purchasing options to fall back to.

