---@field MaintenanceOptions? aws.ec2.InstanceMaintenanceOptionsRequest The maintenance and recovery options for the instance.
---@field DisableApiStop? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether an instance is enabled for stop protection. For more information, see Enable stop protection for your EC2 instances.
---@field EnablePrimaryIpv6? aws.ec2.Boolean If you’re launching an instance into a dual-stack or IPv6-only subnet, you can enable assigning a primary IPv6 address. A primary IPv6 address is an IPv6 GUA address associated with an ENI that you have enabled to use a primary IPv6 address. Use this option if an instance relies on its IPv6 address not changing. When you launch the instance, Amazon Web Services will automatically assign an IPv6 ...
---@field NetworkPerformanceOptions? aws.ec2.InstanceNetworkPerformanceOptionsRequest Contains settings for the network performance options for the instance.
