---The Amazon Inspector scan-result criteria that an AMI must meet to be allowed. The criteria can limit the highest finding severity. They can also limit, for each severity, the days since Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available.
---@class aws.ec2.ScanResultCondition
---@field MaxDaysSinceLastFindingScan? aws.ec2.MaxDaysSinceLastFindingScanValue The maximum number of days that have elapsed since Amazon Inspector last scanned the AMI. For example, a value of 7 allows AMIs that were scanned within the last 7 days. AMIs that Amazon Inspector has not scanned are not allowed.
---@field MaximumSeverityLabel? aws.ec2.SeverityLabel The maximum severity that an AMI's Amazon Inspector findings can have for the AMI to be allowed. Findings count whether or not a fix is available. For example, a value of medium allows AMIs whose highest severity is informational, low, or medium.
---@field MaxDaysSinceInformationalFixAvailable? aws.ec2.MaxDaysSinceFixAvailableValue The maximum number of days since Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for an informational severity finding on the AMI. For example, a value of 7 does not allow an AMI if Amazon Inspector reported such a fix more than 7 days ago.
---@field MaxDaysSinceLowFixAvailable? aws.ec2.MaxDaysSinceFixAvailableValue The maximum number of days since Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for a low severity finding on the AMI. For example, a value of 7 does not allow an AMI if Amazon Inspector reported such a fix more than 7 days ago.
---@field MaxDaysSinceMediumFixAvailable? aws.ec2.MaxDaysSinceFixAvailableValue The maximum number of days since Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for a medium severity finding on the AMI. For example, a value of 7 does not allow an AMI if Amazon Inspector reported such a fix more than 7 days ago.
---@field MaxDaysSinceHighFixAvailable? aws.ec2.MaxDaysSinceFixAvailableValue The maximum number of days since Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for a high severity finding on the AMI. For example, a value of 7 does not allow an AMI if Amazon Inspector reported such a fix more than 7 days ago.
---@field MaxDaysSinceCriticalFixAvailable? aws.ec2.MaxDaysSinceFixAvailableValue The maximum number of days since Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for a critical severity finding on the AMI. For example, a value of 7 does not allow an AMI if Amazon Inspector reported such a fix more than 7 days ago.

