---The Amazon Inspector scan results for an AMI. This information is present only for AMIs that Amazon Inspector has scanned.
---@class aws.ec2.ScanResults
---@field HighestFindingSeverityLabel? aws.ec2.SeverityLabel The highest severity among the AMI's Amazon Inspector findings, whether or not a fix is available.
---@field FindingScanDate? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The date and time, in the ISO 8601 format in the UTC time zone (YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ), of the most recent Amazon Inspector scan of the AMI.
---@field InformationalFixAvailableSince? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The earliest date and time, in the ISO 8601 format in the UTC time zone (YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ), at which Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for an informational severity finding on the AMI. This value is present only if the AMI has at least one informational severity finding with a fix available. Amazon Inspector recomputes this value on each scan.
---@field LowFixAvailableSince? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The earliest date and time, in the ISO 8601 format in the UTC time zone (YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ), at which Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for a low severity finding on the AMI. This value is present only if the AMI has at least one low severity finding with a fix available. Amazon Inspector recomputes this value on each scan.
---@field MediumFixAvailableSince? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The earliest date and time, in the ISO 8601 format in the UTC time zone (YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ), at which Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for a medium severity finding on the AMI. This value is present only if the AMI has at least one medium severity finding with a fix available. Amazon Inspector recomputes this value on each scan.
---@field HighFixAvailableSince? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The earliest date and time, in the ISO 8601 format in the UTC time zone (YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ), at which Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for a high severity finding on the AMI. This value is present only if the AMI has at least one high severity finding with a fix available. Amazon Inspector recomputes this value on each scan.
---@field CriticalFixAvailableSince? aws.ec2.MillisecondDateTime The earliest date and time, in the ISO 8601 format in the UTC time zone (YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.sssZ), at which Amazon Inspector reported a fix as available for a critical severity finding on the AMI. This value is present only if the AMI has at least one critical severity finding with a fix available. Amazon Inspector recomputes this value on each scan.

