---Contains information about a NAT gateway rule for a transit gateway attachment, including the rule number, the source CIDR block, the translated CIDR block, and the state of the rule.
---@class aws.ec2.TransitGatewayNatRule
---@field RuleNumber? aws.ec2.Integer The rule number.
---@field MatchSourceCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv4 CIDR block of the source addresses to translate.
---@field NatCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv4 CIDR block that the transit gateway translates the source addresses to.
---@field State? aws.ec2.TransitGatewayNatRuleState The state of the NAT gateway rule. The possible values are:

---@alias aws.ec2.TransitGatewayNatRuleList aws.ec2.TransitGatewayNatRule[]

---Describes a NAT gateway rule to apply to a transit gateway attachment. A NAT gateway rule translates source addresses in the MatchSourceCidr range to the corresponding addresses in the NatCidr range.
---@class aws.ec2.TransitGatewayNatRuleRequest
---@field RuleNumber? aws.ec2.Integer The rule number. Valid values are 1 to 32766. Each rule number must be unique within the request.
---@field MatchSourceCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv4 CIDR block of the source addresses to translate. The CIDR block can't overlap the multicast range (224.0.0.0/4) or the link-local range (169.254.0.0/16).
---@field NatCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv4 CIDR block to translate the source addresses to. The CIDR block must be in a private (RFC 1918) or shared address space (RFC 6598) range, and must have the same prefix length as MatchSourceCidr. The CIDR blocks in the rules for an attachment can't overlap each other.

---@alias aws.ec2.TransitGatewayNatRuleRequestList aws.ec2.TransitGatewayNatRuleRequest[]

---@alias aws.ec2.TransitGatewayNatRuleState "pending"|"activated"|"deactivated"|"deleting"

---@alias aws.ec2.TransitGatewayNetworkInterfaceIdList aws.ec2.NetworkInterfaceId[]

---Describes the options for a transit gateway.
---@class aws.ec2.TransitGatewayOptions
---@field AmazonSideAsn? aws.ec2.Long A private Autonomous System Number (ASN) for the Amazon side of a BGP session. The range is 64512 to 65534 for 16-bit ASNs and 4200000000 to 4294967294 for 32-bit ASNs.
---@field TransitGatewayCidrBlocks? aws.ec2.ValueStringList The transit gateway CIDR blocks.
---@field AutoAcceptSharedAttachments? aws.ec2.AutoAcceptSharedAttachmentsValue Indicates whether attachment requests are automatically accepted.
---@field DefaultRouteTableAssociation? aws.ec2.DefaultRouteTableAssociationValue Indicates whether resource attachments are automatically associated with the default association route table. Enabled by default. Either defaultRouteTableAssociation or defaultRouteTablePropagation must be set to enable for Amazon Web Services Transit Gateway to create the default transit gateway route table.
---@field AssociationDefaultRouteTableId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the default association route table.
---@field DefaultRouteTablePropagation? aws.ec2.DefaultRouteTablePropagationValue Indicates whether resource attachments automatically propagate routes to the default propagation route table. Enabled by default. If defaultRouteTablePropagation is set to enable, Amazon Web Services Transit Gateway creates the default transit gateway route table.
---@field PropagationDefaultRouteTableId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the default propagation route table.
---@field VpnEcmpSupport? aws.ec2.VpnEcmpSupportValue Indicates whether Equal Cost Multipath Protocol support is enabled.
---@field DnsSupport? aws.ec2.DnsSupportValue Indicates whether DNS support is enabled.
---@field SecurityGroupReferencingSupport? aws.ec2.SecurityGroupReferencingSupportValue Enables you to reference a security group across VPCs attached to a transit gateway to simplify security group management.
---@field MulticastSupport? aws.ec2.MulticastSupportValue Indicates whether multicast is enabled on the transit gateway
---@field EncryptionSupport? aws.ec2.EncryptionSupport Defines if the Transit Gateway supports VPC Encryption Control.

