---Describes VPN connection options.
---@class aws.ec2.VpnConnectionOptions
---@field EnableAcceleration? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether acceleration is enabled for the VPN connection.
---@field StaticRoutesOnly? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicates whether the VPN connection uses static routes only. Static routes must be used for devices that don't support BGP.
---@field LocalIpv4NetworkCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv4 CIDR on the customer gateway (on-premises) side of the VPN connection.
---@field RemoteIpv4NetworkCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv4 CIDR on the Amazon Web Services side of the VPN connection.
---@field LocalIpv6NetworkCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv6 CIDR on the customer gateway (on-premises) side of the VPN connection.
---@field RemoteIpv6NetworkCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv6 CIDR on the Amazon Web Services side of the VPN connection.
---@field OutsideIpAddressType? aws.ec2.String The type of IPv4 address assigned to the outside interface of the customer gateway.
---@field TransportTransitGatewayAttachmentId? aws.ec2.String The transit gateway attachment ID in use for the VPN tunnel.
---@field TunnelInsideIpVersion? aws.ec2.TunnelInsideIpVersion Indicates whether the VPN tunnels process IPv4 or IPv6 traffic.
---@field TunnelOptions? aws.ec2.TunnelOptionsList Indicates the VPN tunnel options.
---@field TunnelBandwidth? aws.ec2.VpnTunnelBandwidth The configured bandwidth for the VPN tunnel. Represents the current throughput capacity setting for the tunnel connection. standard tunnel bandwidth supports up to 1.25 Gbps per tunnel while large supports up to 5 Gbps per tunnel. If no tunnel bandwidth was specified for the connection, standard is used as the default value.

---Describes VPN connection options.
---@class aws.ec2.VpnConnectionOptionsSpecification
---@field EnableAcceleration? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicate whether to enable acceleration for the VPN connection.
---@field TunnelInsideIpVersion? aws.ec2.TunnelInsideIpVersion|string Indicate whether the VPN tunnels process IPv4 or IPv6 traffic.
---@field TunnelOptions? aws.ec2.VpnTunnelOptionsSpecificationsList The tunnel options for the VPN connection.
---@field LocalIpv4NetworkCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv4 CIDR on the customer gateway (on-premises) side of the VPN connection.
---@field RemoteIpv4NetworkCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv4 CIDR on the Amazon Web Services side of the VPN connection.
---@field LocalIpv6NetworkCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv6 CIDR on the customer gateway (on-premises) side of the VPN connection.
---@field RemoteIpv6NetworkCidr? aws.ec2.String The IPv6 CIDR on the Amazon Web Services side of the VPN connection.
---@field OutsideIpAddressType? aws.ec2.String The type of IP address assigned to the outside interface of the customer gateway device.
---@field TransportTransitGatewayAttachmentId? aws.ec2.TransitGatewayAttachmentId The transit gateway attachment ID to use for the VPN tunnel.
---@field TunnelBandwidth? aws.ec2.VpnTunnelBandwidth|string The desired bandwidth specification for the VPN tunnel, used when creating or modifying VPN connection options to set the tunnel's throughput capacity. standard supports up to 1.25 Gbps per tunnel, while large supports up to 5 Gbps per tunnel. The default value is standard. Existing VPN connections without a bandwidth setting will automatically default to standard.
---@field StaticRoutesOnly? aws.ec2.Boolean Indicate whether the VPN connection uses static routes only. If you are creating a VPN connection for a device that does not support BGP, you must specify true. Use CreateVpnConnectionRoute to create a static route.

---@alias aws.ec2.VpnEcmpSupportValue "enable"|"disable"

---Describes a virtual private gateway.
---@class aws.ec2.VpnGateway
---@field AmazonSideAsn? aws.ec2.Long The private Autonomous System Number (ASN) for the Amazon side of a BGP session.
---@field Tags? aws.ec2.TagList Any tags assigned to the virtual private gateway.
---@field VpnGatewayId? aws.ec2.String The ID of the virtual private gateway.
---@field State? aws.ec2.VpnState The current state of the virtual private gateway.
---@field Type? aws.ec2.GatewayType The type of VPN connection the virtual private gateway supports.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.ec2.String The Availability Zone where the virtual private gateway was created, if applicable. This field may be empty or not returned.
---@field VpcAttachments? aws.ec2.VpcAttachmentList Any VPCs attached to the virtual private gateway.

---@alias aws.ec2.VpnGatewayId string

---@alias aws.ec2.VpnGatewayIdStringList aws.ec2.VpnGatewayId[]

